BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 788 Tm (How this enforces least privilege:) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 756 Tm (- The service account can only view pods) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 740 Tm (- It cannot delete deployments) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 724 Tm (- It cannot read secrets unless explicitly granted) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 692 Tm (Why this matters:) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 660 Tm (- Limits damage from compromised pods) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 644 Tm (- Prevents accidental misuse) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 628 Tm (- Improves auditability) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 596 Tm (Best practices:) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 564 Tm (- Prefer namespace-scoped `Role` over `ClusterRole` when possible) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 548 Tm (- Avoid broad permissions like `*`) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 532 Tm (- Use separate service accounts for different applications) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 516 Tm (- Review bindings regularly) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 484 Tm (This is a practical and secure way to control access in Kubernetes.) Tj ET
BT /HelveticaBold 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 452 Tm (9. Analyze cost optimization techniques in Kubernetes clusters) Tj ET
BT /HelveticaBold 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 434 Tm (and their impact on performance and efficiency.) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 400 Tm (Kubernetes can become expensive when workloads request too many resources,) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 384 Tm (nodes remain underutilized, or unused resources stay active.) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 352 Tm (#### Key cost optimization techniques) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 320 Tm (1. Right-size requests and limits) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 304 Tm (Set CPU and memory values based on actual usage rather than guesswork.) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 272 Tm (Impact:) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 256 Tm (Reduces over-provisioning and improves node utilization.) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 224 Tm (2. Monitor pod and node usage) Tj ET
BT /Courier 9 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 192 Tm (kubectl top pod) Tj ET
BT /Courier 9 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 179 Tm (kubectl top node) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 134 Tm (Impact:) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 118 Tm (Helps identify waste, overloaded pods, and idle nodes.) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 86 Tm (3. Scale based on demand) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 70 Tm (Use HPA or manual scaling to increase pods during peak traffic and reduce them) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 471 28 Tm (Page 27 of 29) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
31 0 obj
<< /Length 2620 >>
stream
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 788 Tm (during low traffic.) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 756 Tm (Impact:) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 740 Tm (Matches cost to workload demand.) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 708 Tm (4. Clean unused resources) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 692 Tm (Remove unused namespaces, orphaned services, idle pods, and old volumes.) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 660 Tm (Impact:) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 644 Tm (Eliminates hidden recurring cost.) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 612 Tm (5. Manage storage carefully) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 596 Tm (Delete unused PVCs and choose suitable storage classes.) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 564 Tm (Impact:) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 548 Tm (Prevents paying for unnecessary storage capacity.) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 516 Tm (#### Performance trade-off) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 484 Tm (Cost optimization should not become under-provisioning.) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 452 Tm (If requests are set too low:) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 420 Tm (- pods may be throttled) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 404 Tm (- performance may drop) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 388 Tm (- instability may increase) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 356 Tm (So the goal is not simply to reduce resources, but to right-size them.) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 324 Tm (Example:) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 308 Tm (If a pod consistently uses only 200m CPU but requests 1000m CPU, lowering the) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 292 Tm (request can free space for other workloads and may allow the cluster to run on) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 276 Tm (fewer nodes.) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 244 Tm (In small clusters, these simple optimization practices provide major savings) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 228 Tm (without requiring advanced commercial tooling.) Tj ET
BT /HelveticaBold 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 196 Tm (10. Analyze how Architecture Decision Records \(ADRs\) improve) Tj ET
BT /HelveticaBold 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 178 Tm (maintainability, traceability, and decision-making in) Tj ET
BT /HelveticaBold 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 160 Tm (Kubernetes-based systems.) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 126 Tm (An Architecture Decision Record, or ADR, is a short document that captures:) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 94 Tm (- the context of a problem) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 78 Tm (- the decision taken) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 471 28 Tm (Page 28 of 29) Tj ET
endstream
