32 0 obj
<< /Length 3008 >>
stream
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 788 Tm (- the status) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 772 Tm (- the consequences) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 740 Tm (In Kubernetes-based systems, teams make many recurring decisions about) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 724 Tm (deployment style, security controls, observability, and cost management. If) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 708 Tm (these choices are not documented, future team members may not understand why) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 692 Tm (the system was designed in a particular way.) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 660 Tm (#### How ADRs improve maintainability) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 628 Tm (- They preserve architectural knowledge) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 612 Tm (- They reduce confusion when team members change) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 596 Tm (- They help future engineers maintain the system without repeating old) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 580 Tm (  mistakes) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 548 Tm (#### How ADRs improve traceability) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 516 Tm (- They record why a decision was made) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 500 Tm (- They connect system behavior back to a documented reason) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 484 Tm (- They make audits and reviews easier) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 452 Tm (#### How ADRs improve decision-making) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 420 Tm (- Teams can compare new proposals against past reasoning) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 404 Tm (- Superseded decisions remain visible instead of being forgotten) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 388 Tm (- Discussions become more objective because context is documented) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 356 Tm (Example ADR topic:) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 340 Tm (?Use Kubernetes Secrets with Sealed Secrets for GitOps-managed credentials.?) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 308 Tm (Possible content:) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 276 Tm (- Context: plain YAML secrets are risky in Git) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 260 Tm (- Decision: use Sealed Secrets) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 244 Tm (- Consequences: safer Git storage, extra controller dependency) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 212 Tm (Best practices:) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 180 Tm (- Keep ADRs short and clear) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 164 Tm (- Write them when the decision is made) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 148 Tm (- Store them in the repository, such as `/docs/adr/`) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 132 Tm (- Do not delete old ADRs; mark them as superseded) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 100 Tm (Therefore, ADRs improve long-term system quality by making important) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 84 Tm (architecture choices visible, understandable, and reviewable.) Tj ET
BT /Helvetica 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 471 28 Tm (Page 29 of 29) Tj ET
endstream
